>UpsCommOk</Text><Enum>1</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[The communication path to the UPS is OK.]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>UpsCommFailed</Text><Enum>2</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[The communication path to the UPS has failed.]]></Comment></EnumInfo></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Vanguard.Tc2_IoFunctions">E_UpsPowerStatus</Name><BitSize>16</BitSize><BaseType>INT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>PowerUnknownStatus</Text><Enum>0</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[The status of power is unknown.]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>PowerOnLine</Text><Enum>1</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Power is OK.]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>PowerOnBattery</Text><Enum>2</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[A power failure has occurred.]]></Comment></EnumInfo></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Vanguard.Tc2_IoFunctions">ST_UPSStatus</Name><BitSize>2784</BitSize><SubItem><Name>Vendor</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Vendor name ]]></Comment><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>Model</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Model name ]]></Comment><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>648</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>FirmwareRev</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Reports the UPS firmware revision as a displayable string. ]]></Comment><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>1296</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>SerialNumber</Name><Type>STRING(80)</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Reports the UPS serial number as a displayable string.]]></Comment><BitSize>648</BitSize><BitOffs>1944</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>BatteryLifePercent</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ The percent of battery capacity remaining in the UPS, represented as a value in the range of 0 through 100. ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>2592</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>BatteryLifeTime</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ The amount of remaining UPS run time, in minutes.]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>2624</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>eBatteryStatus</Name><Type Namespace="Vanguard.Tc2_IoFunctions">E_BatteryStatus</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ The current status of the UPS batteries. ]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>2656</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>eCommStatus</Name><Type Namespace="Vanguard.Tc2_IoFunctions">E_UpsCommStatus</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ The status of the communication path to the UPS. ]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>2672</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>ePowerStatus</Name><Type Namespace="Vanguard.Tc2_IoFunctions">E_UpsPowerStatus</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Reports the status of utility-supplied power into the UPS. ]]></Comment><BitSize>16</BitSize><BitOffs>2688</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nPowerFailCnt</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Power fail counter ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>2720</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>dwChargeFlags</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><Comment><![CDATA[	Most reserved for future use. Battery charge status flags. This member can be one or more of the following values.
		0:		Unknown status (none status information)
		1: 		High (bit 0 is set)
		2: 		Low (bit 1 is set) 
		4: 		Critical (bit 2 is set)
		8:		Charging (bit 3 is set)
		- 		- (bits 4..6 reserved)
		128:	No battery (bit 7 is set)
		256:    UPS fan error (bit 8 is set)
		-       - (bit 9 reserved)
