ame Namespace="Tc3_Vision">ETcVnThresholdType</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Offers threshold types. ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DINT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>TCVN_TT_BINARY</Text><Enum>0</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Binary threshold ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TCVN_TT_BINARY_INV</Text><Enum>1</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Inverted binary threshold ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TCVN_TT_TRUNC</Text><Enum>2</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Truncated threshold (pixels > thresh are set to thresh, others keep their value) ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TCVN_TT_TOZERO</Text><Enum>3</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ To zero threshold (pixels < thresh are set to zero, others keep their value) ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TCVN_TT_TOZERO_INV</Text><Enum>4</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Inverted to zero threshold (pixels > thresh are set to zero, others keep their value) ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TCVN_TT_OTSU_BINARY</Text><Enum>8</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Binary threshold with the threshold value selected according to the Otsu algorithm ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TCVN_TT_OTSU_BINARY_INV</Text><Enum>9</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Inverted binary threshold with the threshold value selected according to the Otsu algorithm ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TCVN_TT_OTSU_TRUNC</Text><Enum>10</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Truncated threshold with the threshold value selected according to the Otsu algorithm ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TCVN_TT_OTSU_TOZERO</Text><Enum>11</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ To zero threshold with the threshold value selected according to the Otsu algorithm ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TCVN_TT_OTSU_TOZERO_INV</Text><Enum>12</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Inverted to zero threshold with the threshold value selected according to the Otsu algorithm ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TCVN_TT_TRIANGLE_BINARY</Text><Enum>16</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Binary threshold with the threshold value selected according to the Triangle algorithm ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TCVN_TT_TRIANGLE_BINARY_INV</Text><Enum>17</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Inverted binary threshold with the threshold value selected according to the Triangle algorithm ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TCVN_TT_TRIANGLE_TRUNC</Text><Enum>18</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Truncated threshold with the threshold value selected according to the Triangle algorithm ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TCVN_TT_TRIANGLE_TOZERO</Text><Enum>19</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ To zero threshold with the threshold value selected according to the Triangle algorithm ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TCVN_TT_TRIANGLE_TOZERO_INV</Text><Enum>20</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Inverted to zero threshold with the threshold value selected according to the Triangle algorithm ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>Namespace</Name><Value>Tc3_Vision</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Tc3_Vision">ETcVnBlobCombination</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Offers multiple blob contours to choose from, which should be returned in a multi-threshold scenario (used in TcVnParamsBlobDetection, which in return is used in F_VN_DetectBlobs). ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BaseType>DINT</BaseType><EnumInfo><Text>TCVN_BC_SMALLEST</Text><Enum>0</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Returns the smallest blob contour. ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TCVN_BC_LARGEST</Text><Enum>1</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Returns the largest blob contour. ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TCVN_BC_MIN_THRESHOLD</Text><Enum>2</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Returns the blob contour for the minimum threshold. ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TCVN_BC_MAX_THRESHOLD</Text><Enum>3</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Returns the blob contour for the maximum threshold. ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><EnumInfo><Text>TCVN_BC_MEDIAN_THRESHOLD</Text><Enum>4</Enum><Comment><![CDATA[ Returns the blob contour for the median threshold. ]]></Comment></EnumInfo><Properties><Property><Name>Namespace</Name><Value>Tc3_Vision</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Tc3_Vision" IecLibraryType="true">TcVnParamsBlobDetection</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Offers parameters for blob detection ]]></Comment><BitSize>640</BitSize><SubItem><Name>bFilterByArea</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Enable filtering by area (fMinArea <= area <= fMaxArea); strongly recommended to activate for filtering noise with fMinArea. ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs><Default><Bool>true</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bFilterByCircularity</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Enable filtering by circularity (fMinCircularity <= circularity(4pi * area / perimeter^2) <= fMaxCircularity). ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>8</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bFilterByConvexity</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Enable filtering by convexity (fMinConvexity <= convexity(area / hullArea) <= fMaxConvexity). ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>16</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bFilterByEccentricity</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Enable filtering by eccentricity (fMinEccentricity <= eccentricity <= fMaxEccentricity). ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>24</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bFilterByInertiaRatio</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Enable filtering by inertia ratio (fMinInertiaRatio <= inertia ratio <= fMaxInertiaRatio). ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fMinArea</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Min estimated blob area in pixel ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Default><Value>10</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fMaxArea</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Max estimated blob area in pixel ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs><Default><Value>100000000</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fMinCircularity</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Min circularity (1.0: ideal circle, < 1: less circular, 0: not circular at all) ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs><Default><Value>0</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fMaxCircularity</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Max circularity (1.0: ideal circle, < 1: less circular, 0: not circular at all) ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>160</BitOffs><Default><Value>1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fMinConvexity</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Min convexity (1.0: blob fully convex, < 1: less convex) ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>192</BitOffs><Default><Value>0</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fMaxConvexity</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Max convexity (1.0: blob fully convex, < 1: less convex) ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>224</BitOffs><Default><Value>1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fMinEccentricity</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Min eccentricity (0.0: circular, 1.0: linear) ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>256</BitOffs><Default><Value>0</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fMaxEccentricity</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Max eccentricity (0.0: circular, 1.0: linear) ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>288</BitOffs><Default><Value>1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fMinInertiaRatio</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Min inertia ratio (1.0: equal width and height, 0.0: linear) ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>320</BitOffs><Default><Value>0</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fMaxInertiaRatio</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Max inertia ratio (1.0: equal width and height, 0.0: linear) ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>352</BitOffs><Default><Value>1</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>eThresholdType</Name><Type Namespace="Tc3_Vision">ETcVnThresholdType</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Threshold type for internally applied threshold method (OTSU_XXX only supported for USINT images). ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>384</BitOffs><Default><EnumText>ETcVnThresholdType.TCVN_TT_BINARY</EnumText></Default><Properties><Property><Name>Namespace</Name><Value>Tc3_Vision</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fMinThreshold</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Threshold to start with (if fThresholdStep > 0, otherwise this is the only threshold used). ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>416</BitOffs><Default><Value>30</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fMaxThreshold</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Threshold to end with (if fThresholdStep > 0, otherwise this value is not used). ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>448</BitOffs><Default><Value>225</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fThresholdStep</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Sets to 0 if only 1 threshold should be used (much faster than multiple thresholds and combining the results). ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>480</BitOffs><Default><Value>0</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fMinBlobDistance</Name><Type>REAL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Minimum distance between the center points of two different blobs (only used if fThresholdStep > 0; if distance < fMinBlobDistance, the blobs are treated as the same). ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>512</BitOffs><Default><Value>5</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>nMinRepeatability</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Minimum number of threshold steps, for which the same contour has to be detected (only used if fThresholdStep > 0; same means center point distance < fMinBlobDistance). ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>544</BitOffs><Default><Value>2</Value></Default></SubItem><SubItem><Name>eBlobCombination</Name><Type Namespace="Tc3_Vision">ETcVnBlobCombination</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Selects, which of the multi-threshold blob contours should be returned. ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>576</BitOffs><Default><EnumText>ETcVnBlobCombination.TCVN_BC_MEDIAN_THRESHOLD</EnumText></Default><Properties><Property><Name>Namespace</Name><Value>Tc3_Vision</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>bExcludeBorderBlobs</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ If true, blobs touching the image border are excluded from the results. ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>608</BitOffs><Default><Bool>false</Bool></Default></SubItem><Properties><Property><Name>Namespace</Name><Value>Tc3_Vision</Value></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Tc2_Utilities">PROFILERSTRUCT</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Profiler status information ]]></Comment><BitSize>160</BitSize><SubItem><Name>LastExecTime</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ [us]]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>0</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>MinExecTime</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ [us]]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>32</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>MaxExecTime</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ [us]]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>AverageExecTime</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ [us]]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs></SubItem><SubItem><Name>MeasureCycle</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs></SubItem></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Tc2_System">FW_GetCpuAccount</Name><BitSize>128</BitSize><SubItem><Name>dwCpuAccount</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property><Property><Name>conditionalshow</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Tc2_System">GETCPUACCOUNT</Name><Comment><![CDATA[	The PLC task cycle ticker can be read with this function block. 
	The PLC task cycle ticker is only incremented while the task is being executed. 
	The numerical value is a 32 bit integer, which, independently of the CPU's internal clock rate, is output in a form converted into 100ns ticks. 
	The number is refreshed to a precision of 100ns every time the PLC task is called, and can be used, for instance, for timing purposes. 
	One unit is equivalent to 100 ns.]]></Comment><BitSize>256</BitSize><SubItem><Name>cpuAccountDW</Name><Type>UDINT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ The current value of the PLC task ticker ]]></Comment><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>fbGetCpuAccount</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_System">FW_GetCpuAccount</Type><BitSize>128</BitSize><BitOffs>128</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>conditionalshow</Name></Property></Properties></SubItem><Properties><Property><Name>PouType</Name><Value>FunctionBlock</Value></Property><Property><Name>conditionalshow_all_locals</Name></Property></Properties></DataType><DataType><Name Namespace="Tc2_Utilities">Profiler</Name><Comment><![CDATA[ Code execution profiler function block ]]></Comment><BitSize>4352</BitSize><SubItem><Name>START</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Rising edge starts measurement and falling stops]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>64</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>RESET</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Resets previous measure ]]></Comment><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>72</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Input</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>BUSY</Name><Type>BOOL</Type><BitSize>8</BitSize><BitOffs>80</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>DATA</Name><Type Namespace="Tc2_Utilities">PROFILERSTRUCT</Type><Comment><![CDATA[ Profiler/measure output data ]]></Comment><BitSize>160</BitSize><BitOffs>96</BitOffs><Properties><Property><Name>ItemType</Name><Value>Output</Value></Property></Properties></SubItem><SubItem><Name>MAX_DATABUFF_SIZE</Name><Type>DWORD</Type><BitSize>32</BitSize><BitOffs>256</BitOffs><Default><Value>100</Value></Default><Properties><Property><Name>condi